WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.970
This wildly profitable socially themed horror-comedy
was one of the biggest success stories of

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.100
2017.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.139
Still, it's easy to get a little lost in all
the action, and hard-hitting subtext, on the

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.700
screen during the final act.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.880
To help you make sense of it all, here's Get
Out's ending explained.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:17.920
"Hi.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.820
I'm Roman Armitage and if you're watching
this, you're probably wondering what's going

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.320
on."

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.420
The ultimate reveal at the end of Get Out
is so organically earned that the weight of

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.660
it can be hard to understand on first viewing.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.200
When Chris goes to meet his white girlfriend
Rose's parents for the first time, he's apprehensive.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.180
"You said I was the first black guy you ever
dated."

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.190
"Yeah, so what?"

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.040
"Yeah, so this is uncharted territory for
me.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.300
You know, I don't wanna get chased off your
front lawn with a shotgun."

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.180
At first his fears seem ridiculous since Missy
and Dean seem perfectly nice, if awkward.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.280
However, Dean drops some early foreshadowing
when he reminisces about when his father lost

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.880
a race to Jesse Owens.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.060
"Tough break for your dad though."

00:00:59.060 --> 00:00:59.560
"Yeah.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.900
He almost got over it."

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.520
As the audience and Chris soon learn, the
Armitages and their friends are planning to

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.500
steal Chris' body as part of a plan to live
forever in the bodies of kidnapped black people.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.360
Dean's musing about his father's loss to a
black man hints early on that the Armitages

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.780
aren't exactly as jovial as they seem.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.740
Later in the film, Chris is hypnotized against
his will by Missy and introduced to "The Sunken

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:26.240
Place."

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.560
"Now you're in the sunken place."

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.920
What exactly is the Sunken Place?

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.100
It's a visual display of what happens when
Chris is paralyzed through hypnosis, but according

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.940
to director Jordan Peele, it also represents
the reality of living as a marginalized person.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.140
Peele tweeted:

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.460
"We are all in the Sunken Place...

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.540
We're marginalized.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.600
No matter how hard we scream, the system silences
us."

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:00.320
Unfortunately, Chris soon learns that racism
is a family business and that his girlfriend

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.780
Rose is a willing participant in her family's
crimes.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.289
For years, she's been luring black people
back to her family's home to be hypnotized

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:08.440
for dark purposes.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:13.260
As Chris wakes up paralyzed in a chair, he
finds out just how terrifying the Armitage

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.700
family really is.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.500
A video reveals that the family is part of
a cult called the Order of Coagula, originally

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.940
led by Rose's grandfather.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:26.040
The video goes on to say that the Order of
Coagula developed a method of life extension

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.520
through brain transplants.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.409
Young black people were sought out for these
operations for their perceived superior physical

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:33.040
traits.

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:37.560
The black people are lobotomized, preserving
only a shadow of the host's consciousness,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.180
forever doomed to reside as a paralyzed passenger
in its own body.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.880
Their brains are replaced with the consciousness
of rich, old white people interested in immortality.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.820
It's already been established that Chris'
response to hypnosis is to panic scratch at

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:52.900
a chair's upholstery.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.340
This winds up being his saving grace.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.380
Chris is able to pull some cotton from the
chair he's been confined to and stuff it in

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:02.500
his ears so that he isn't affected by the
hypnotic sound.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:07.580
After gaining the upper hand on the Armitages
in a satisfyingly violent sequence, Chris

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.480
gets in a car and tries to escape.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.240
In the process, he comes to a final confrontation
with his former girlfriend Rose.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.140
By the end of it, Rose lies wounded on the
ground telling Chris that she still loves

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:18.640
him.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.760
"I'm so sorry.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.040
It's me.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.500
I, I love you, I love you."

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.640
Chris sees through the lie, and begins to
strangle her, but after their time together,

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.880
he just can't bring himself to go through
with it.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.060
As he lets up on Rose, we see a police car's
red and blue lights flashing.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.080
Earlier in the film, Rose and Chris are pulled
over.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:46.100
Despite the fact that Rose is driving, the
police officer asks to see Chris' ID, and

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.460
he hands it over, sadly accustomed to being
profiled by the law.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.760
So when the police lights flash in the movie's
final moments, we fear that Chris will be

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.500
shot or railroaded into prison by a racist
police officer.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:03.180
Luckily, it isn't a police car, but rather
a TSA vehicle driven by Chris' pal Rod.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.680
Chris walks away from Rose, leaving her to
possibly die from her wounds, and gets in

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.460
Rod's car, finally free from the Armitage's
twisted scheme.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:16.860
It's a mostly happy ending, but Peele nearly
ripped out audiences' hearts with an alternate

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.560
deleted ending.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:23.260
In the alternate ending, it's not Rod who
turns up to save the day, but the actual police.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.740
Chris is blamed for the deaths at the Armitage
house and arrested, and the scene cuts to

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.000
Rod visiting Chris in prison.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:33.480
The movie ends with Chris accepting his fate
in prison, secure in the knowledge that at

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.080
least he stopped what was happening.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.020
"I'm good.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.440
I stopped it.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:41.720
You know?"

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.880
But as Chris hangs up the phone, we can see
the dozens of black men that are in prison

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.980
with him, and we know that Chris didn't really
stop anything; he just stopped one particularly

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.880
fantastical symptom of racism.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:58.260
Ultimately, Peele went with the theatrical
ending because he felt like the deleted one

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.940
was just too heavy for an audience that needed
a break.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.500
He told Variety that:

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.540
"It was very clear that the ending needed
to transform into something that gives us

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:11.140
a hero, that gives us an escape, gives us
a positive feeling when we leave this movie."

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.580
In Get Out, the Order of Coagula are not the
kind of societal outcast racists that are

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.540
usually depicted in movies.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.630
These are socially accepted, otherwise-upstanding-citizen
racists, who keep their true evil hidden by

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.980
falsehoods and platitudes.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:30.380
"Don't, please don't lump me in with that,
you know, I could give a s--- what color you

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.200
are, you know."

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:36.700
By revealing their professed admiration for
the black race as fetishistic and opportunistic,

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:41.160
Peele revealed an unspoken, larger truth that
resonated with audiences worldwide.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.960
Using the microaggressions that people of
color deal with in their everyday lives as

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:51.270
the signals for more sinister motives, Peele
created a story that succeeds both as an engrossing

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:53.880
thriller and as a pointed social commentary.

